{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"9LesM9ObiAxw"},"source":["# Team member(s):\n","\n","If you export an `.ipynb` file from Kaggle, upon submitting your code on Canvas, please type the names of the team members here:\n","\n","- Member 1:\n","- Member 2:"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"yeNXcx_niAxw"},"source":["### UMKC Fall 2025 CS 5590/Math 5555 Final project advanced starter 2\n","\n","This is the advanced starter code for the final project. Please walk it through.\n","You can download this starter as a notebook and upload it to Colab, or directly run it on Kaggle.\n","Do not attempt to run the code locally unless there is a GPU supporting CUDA.\n","All the given models are fairly large (\u003e 10 million parameters) and we only about 30 GPU hours on Kaggle per week.\n","So please plan accordingly and do not start the final project in the last two weeks.\n","\n","The end date of this competition is **Dec 20, 2025**.\n","\n","The due date for submitting the final project report is **Dec 21, 2025**.\n","\n","## Changes from the advanced starter:\n","- A K-fold validation strategy is added: monitoring the accuracy on 1-fold.\n","- A variant of SGD is implemented using Homework 7's problem 1 code with built-in inplace operations.\n","- A learning rate scheduler is added\n","- Tracking and plot the loss function values on train and validation set\n","\n","## Things to try:\n","- Writing your own learning rate scheduler.\n","- Implement [RMSprop](https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=RMSProp#RMSProp) and [AdaDelta](https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=AdaGrad#AdaDelta) with momentum term using `torch.optim`'s `Optimizer` template class.\n","\n","## GPU\n","On the right tab there is a Notebook config option page, there is GPU toggle under \"Notebook options\" tab, clicking the Accelerator drop-down menu will reveal your options. Please choose P100 when you plan to run the code. Kaggle has a Tesla P100 GPU which is better than Colab, but we have only 30 hours of GPU computing time reseting per week. Note this should be more than enough computing power to train the baseline model ResNet"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":14723,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264300368,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"PYYUVvXViAxx","outputId":"65ddcf60-eec9-4e3b-91a8-5bb7e7cdad52"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Collecting torchinfo\n","  Downloading torchinfo-1.8.0-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (21 kB)\n","Downloading torchinfo-1.8.0-py3-none-any.whl (23 kB)\n","Installing collected packages: torchinfo\n","Successfully installed torchinfo-1.8.0\n"]}],"source":["# imports\n","import numpy as np\n","import torch\n","from torch import nn\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader, TensorDataset\n","import torch.nn.functional as F\n","from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Use the ! (bang) prefix to run a shell command inside the notebook\n","!pip install torchinfo"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":52035,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264352405,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"Cffh9Z0FiAxx","outputId":"798329dd-8808-4a59-8d9a-5812d3444493"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Mounted at /content/drive\n","Google Drive mounted successfully.\n","Data loaded successfully from Google Drive.\n","Training data shape: torch.Size([40000, 28, 28])\n"]}],"source":["import torch # Ensure torch is imported if it wasn't already\n","from google.colab import drive\n","\n","# 1. Mount Google Drive\n","# This step requires you to authenticate and click a link/enter a code.\n","drive.mount(\"/content/drive\", force_remount=True)\n","print(\"Google Drive mounted successfully.\")\n","\n","# 2. Define the base path to your data folder\n","# MAKE SURE THIS PATH IS CORRECT for where you saved 'train.pt' and 'test.pt'\n","PATH_TO_DATA = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Colab Notebooks/5590 Project/\"\n","\n","# 3. Load the data using the new Google Drive paths\n","# We use the new PATH_TO_DATA variable to construct the full file path.\n","train = torch.load(f'{PATH_TO_DATA}train.pt')\n","test = torch.load(f'{PATH_TO_DATA}test.pt')\n","\n","# 4. Extract data and targets (This part remains the same)\n","train_data, train_targets = train['data'], train['label']\n","test_data = test['data']\n","\n","print(\"Data loaded successfully from Google Drive.\")\n","print(f\"Training data shape: {train_data.shape}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":13,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264352430,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"vsaN1YbDiAxx","outputId":"7eb4bfde-4d5a-43e4-d614-6c1f7438a673"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["The shapes of train data, train targets, test data are\n"," torch.Size([40000, 28, 28]), torch.Size([40000]), torch.Size([30000, 28, 28]).\n"]}],"source":["# verifying the shapes\n","print(f\"The shapes of train data, train targets, test data are\\n {train_data.size()}, {train_targets.size()}, {test_data.size()}.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"CbvvrvlKiAxx"},"source":["The train set has data and targets given, yet test set has no targets. We have to train models based on the train data to achieve a high score on the leaderboard on the test set."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2JdeBjV5iAxx"},"source":["# Final Project: write an optimizer\n","\n","We will have 3 given CNN models as follows, and we will write our own optimizer(s) using `torch.optim` interface to optimize the given 3 models. You are free to use any techniques learned in the class to optimize the model. The goal is to optimize the model such that the model(s) trained performs good in the test set with unknown targets.\n","\n","\n","## Models:\n","The 3 fixed models we can use are the famous first state-of-art image recognition CNN ResNet: ResNet 18, ResNet 34, and ResNet 509\\ [https://pytorch.org/hub/pytorch_vision_resnet/](https://pytorch.org/hub/pytorch_vision_resnet/). Their settings are in the next cell.\n","The `__init__()` has two parameters:\n","- `block`: the first type is the `BasicBlock` used for building ResNet, defined in the file (`torchvision.models.resnet`). The other type is `Bottleneck` block, which has a more agressive dimension reduction mechanics.\n","- `[2, 2, 2, 2]`: Each number denotes the number of `Bottleneck` or `BasicBlock` modules in a \"stage\". It depends on how deep you want the networks to be. For example, for ResNet18, it is `[2, 2, 2, 2]`; for ResNet34, it is `[3, 4, 6, 3]`.\n","\n","The full code of ResNet is here: [https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/master/torchvision/models/resnet.py](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/master/torchvision/models/resnet.py). We are just gonna import the `torchvision` implementation, and change the first convolutional layer to accept single channel input, and the stride of the first convolutional layer from 2 to 1.\n","\n","## New optimizer to try:\n","\n","#### RMSprop\n","The RMSprop algorithm (non stochastic version) is as follows:\n","\u003e Choose $w_0$, $\\alpha$, $\\gamma$, $\\epsilon$, and let $s^{(-1)} = 1$ \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n","\u003e    For $k=0,1,2, \\cdots, M$\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n","\u003e    \u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;  $s^{(k)} = \\gamma s^{(k-1)} + (1 - \\gamma)\\, \\left|\\nabla f(w^{(k)})\\right|^2$\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n","\u003e    \u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;    $\\displaystyle w^{(k+1)} =  w^{(k)} -  \\frac{\\alpha} {\\sqrt{s^{(k)}+ \\epsilon}} \\nabla f(w^{(k)})$  \n","where $\\left|\\nabla f(w^{(k)})\\right|$ denotes the element-wise magnitude of the gradient vector, and the last line's fraction means element-wise division.\n","\n","An optional optimizer to try would be to adapt RMSprop to the template we have. We are free to implement any from [An overview of gradient descent optimization algorithms](https://www.ruder.io/optimizing-gradient-descent). Note that most of the algorithm have their built-in version in `torch.optim` submodule. If you are able to unwrap the official torch code to fit the template, you are welcome to do that as well.\n","\n","\n","## Validation:\n","\n","Since you do not have access to the target of the test set, to cross-validate your model, you should split the training samples to two sets using the techniques learned in class: one is training dataset, the other is your validation dataset (so that you have access to the targets of this set). This routine is usually used for Kaggle competitions and in the real world model deployment to ensure the trained model has generalizability to the unseen data. In this starter code, **K-fold** is used (yet only trained on 1 fold).\n","\n","## Hyperparameter tuning:\n","Aside from writing our own optimizer, there are quite a few hyperparameter for us to tune to achieve better performance:\n","- learning rate and/or with a scheduler\n","- dropout rate\n","- early stop\n","- other validation strategy based tuning\n","It is okay to use autoML package (H2O, Rapids, Optuna, fast.ai) if you know how to write a wrapper of them using the given model."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":13298,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264365734,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"GwLzInRbiAxy"},"outputs":[],"source":["from torchvision.models.resnet import ResNet, BasicBlock, Bottleneck\n","\n","class MyResNet(ResNet):\n","    def __init__(self,\n","                 block=BasicBlock,\n","                 layers=[2, 2, 2, 2],\n","                 num_classes=10):\n","        super(MyResNet, self).__init__(block,\n","                                       layers,\n","                                       num_classes=num_classes)\n","        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(1, 64, kernel_size=7, stride=1, padding=3,bias=False)\n","\n","        '''\n","        you can modify the layers in this initialization of ResNet if you like\n","        '''\n","\n","# choose 1\n","resnet18 = {\n","    \"block\": BasicBlock,\n","    \"layers\": [2, 2, 2, 2]\n","}\n","\n","resnet34 = {\n","    \"block\": BasicBlock,\n","    \"layers\": [3, 4, 6, 3]\n","}\n","\n","resnet50 = {\n","    \"block\": Bottleneck,\n","    \"layers\": [3, 4, 6, 3]\n","}\n","\n","\n","\n","model = MyResNet(**resnet18)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":11,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264365754,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"qEjql4hOiAxy"},"outputs":[],"source":["from torchinfo import summary # similar function to tensorflow/keras summary for torch"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":692,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366448,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"V2h3QNsLiAxy"},"outputs":[],"source":["batch_size = 64\n","summary(model, input_size=(batch_size, 1, 28, 28), device='cpu'); # (color_channel, 28, 28)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"eOZwJ-y8iAxy"},"source":["A batch size of 1024 of float precision training needs about 4GB of RAM for the GPU."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"i9yrzAj4iAxy"},"source":["# Prepare the train loader"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":17,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366473,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"DCbg0exsiAxy"},"outputs":[],"source":["batch_size = 64\n","\n","skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n","# We take the first fold for this starter code\n","# you can ensemble all folds\n","train_idx, val_idx = next(skf.split(train_data, train_targets))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":12,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366488,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"Kd1Msc5riAxy","outputId":"4e75a2bf-1fd7-462b-baec-27b6a7644e31"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["array([ 0,  1,  3,  4,  5,  6,  7,  8,  9, 10])"]},"execution_count":8,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["train_idx[:10]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":20,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366510,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"1sfZ-u4DiAxy","outputId":"f7d1b578-a905-4965-86e3-891fab1a7491"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["array([ 2, 18, 22, 31, 38, 39, 44, 48, 52, 53])"]},"execution_count":9,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["val_idx[:10]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":54,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366572,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"LjOM5C7eiAxz","outputId":"31e6cdaa-62ff-4870-8aa7-a8ad99ea5049"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["torch.Size([32000, 28, 28])\n"]}],"source":["print(train_data[train_idx].shape)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":159,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366758,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"7qM-JlYuiAxz"},"outputs":[],"source":["# 1fold\n","X_tr = train_data[train_idx][:,None,:,:].float()\n","y_tr = train_targets[train_idx].long()\n","X_val = train_data[val_idx][:,None,:,:].float()\n","y_val = train_targets[val_idx].long()\n","\n","train_set = TensorDataset(X_tr, y_tr)\n","train_loader = DataLoader(train_set, batch_size=batch_size)\n","\n","valid_set = TensorDataset(X_val, y_val)\n","val_loader = DataLoader(valid_set, batch_size=batch_size)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":17,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264366777,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"BW7eiI7qiAxz","outputId":"1dc90940-5b71-497f-f05e-d7fa48144ab2"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["torch.Size([64, 1, 28, 28]) torch.Size([64])\n"]}],"source":["sample = next(iter(train_loader))\n","print(sample[0].size(), sample[1].size())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":494,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264367272,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"G-Wc9eQqiAxz","outputId":"bc0108e0-7af0-40a4-e719-fba963fa9e44"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["torch.Size([64, 10])\n"]}],"source":["with torch.no_grad():\n","    sample_output = model(sample[0]) # verifying the model is okay\n","\n","print(sample_output.size()) # should be (batch_size, n_classes)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":13,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264367287,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"D0IJFIFVLroN"},"outputs":[],"source":["def zeropower_via_newtonschulz5(G, steps: int):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Newton-Schulz iteration to compute the zeroth power / orthogonalization of G. We opt to use a\n","    quintic iteration whose coefficients are selected to maximize the slope at zero. For the purpose\n","    of minimizing steps, it turns out to be empirically effective to keep increasing the slope at\n","    zero even beyond the point where the iteration no longer converges all the way to one everywhere\n","    on the interval. This iteration therefore does not produce UV^T but rather something like US'V^T\n","    where S' is diagonal with S_{ii}' ~ Uniform(0.5, 1.5), which turns out not to hurt model\n","    performance at all relative to UV^T, where USV^T = G is the SVD.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    assert G.ndim \u003e= 2 # batched Muon implementation by @scottjmaddox, and put into practice in the record by @YouJiacheng\n","    a, b, c = (3.4445, -4.7750,  2.0315)\n","    X = G.bfloat16()\n","    if G.size(-2) \u003e G.size(-1):\n","        X = X.mT\n","\n","    # Ensure spectral norm is at most 1\n","    X = X / (X.norm(dim=(-2, -1), keepdim=True) + 1e-7)\n","    # Perform the NS iterations\n","    for _ in range(steps):\n","        A = X @ X.mT\n","        B = b * A + c * A @ A # quintic computation strategy adapted from suggestion by @jxbz, @leloykun, and @YouJiacheng\n","        X = a * X + B @ X\n","\n","    if G.size(-2) \u003e G.size(-1):\n","        X = X.mT\n","    return X"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"kFmIMHGOiAxz"},"source":["# Final project: write our own optimizer\n","\n","In the following cells, we use the `torch.optim` interface to build our own optimizer.\n","The following code is simplified from an early version of [SGD in PyTorch 1.x](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/1.9.0/optim.html?highlight=sgd#torch.optim.SGD)\n","\n","Please refer to the final project page to see requirements of the implementation of a customized optimizer."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":15,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":19,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264367317,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"_hfRcjT7iAxz"},"outputs":[],"source":["from torch.optim import Optimizer\n","import math # Need this import for the step function\n","\n","class Muon(Optimizer):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Muon - MomentUm Orthogonalized by Newton-schulz\n","\n","    https://kellerjordan.github.io/posts/muon/\n","\n","    Muon internally runs standard SGD-momentum, and then performs an orthogonalization post-\n","    processing step, in which each 2D parameter's update is replaced with the nearest orthogonal\n","    matrix. For efficient orthogonalization we use a Newton-Schulz iteration, which has the\n","    advantage that it can be stably run in bfloat16 on the GPU.\n","\n","    Muon should only be used for hidden weight layers. The input embedding, final output layer,\n","    and any internal gains or biases should be optimized using a standard method such as AdamW.\n","    Hidden convolutional weights can be trained using Muon by viewing them as 2D and then\n","    collapsing their last 3 dimensions.\n","\n","    Arguments:\n","        lr: The learning rate, in units of spectral norm per update.\n","        weight_decay: The AdamW-style weight decay.\n","        momentum: The momentum. A value of 0.95 here is usually fine.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    def __init__(self,\n","                 params,\n","                 lr=0.02,\n","                 beta=0.95, # momentum\n","                 ns_steps=5,\n","                 weight_decay=0.0): # may not need in Muon\n","\n","\n","        defaults = dict(lr=lr,\n","                        beta=beta, # \u003c-- The step function reads 'betas' here\n","                        ns_steps=ns_steps,\n","                        weight_decay=weight_decay)\n","        super().__init__(params, defaults)\n","\n","    def step(self, closure=None):\n","        loss = None\n","        for group in self.param_groups:\n","            for p in group['params']:\n","                if p.grad is None:\n","                    continue\n","\n","                if p.ndim \u003c 2:\n","                    continue\n","\n","                grad = p.grad\n","                ns_steps = group['ns_steps']\n","                beta = group['beta']\n","                state = self.state[p]\n","\n","                # State initialization\n","                if len(state) == 0:\n","                    state[\"momentum_buffer\"] = torch.zeros_like(p)\n","\n","                #update = muon_update(grad, state[\"momentum_buffer\"], beta=group[\"momentum\"])\n","                nesterov = True\n","                momentum = state[\"momentum_buffer\"]\n","                momentum.lerp_(grad, 1 - beta)\n","                update = grad.lerp_(momentum, beta) if nesterov else momentum\n","                if update.ndim == 4: # for the case of conv filters\n","                    update = update.view(len(update), -1)\n","                update = zeropower_via_newtonschulz5(update, steps=ns_steps)\n","                update *= max(1, grad.size(-2) / grad.size(-1))**0.5\n","                with torch.no_grad():\n","                    p.mul_(1 - group[\"lr\"] * group[\"weight_decay\"])\n","                    p.add_(update.reshape(p.shape), alpha=-group[\"lr\"])\n","                #p.data.all_gather(params_pad[base_i:base_i + dist.get_world_size()], params_pad[base_i + dist.get_rank()])\n","                \"\"\"\"\n","                exp_avg, exp_avg_sq = state['exp_avg'], state['exp_avg_sq']\n","                beta1, beta2 = group['betas']\n","\n","                state['step'] += 1\n","\n","                exp_avg.mul_(beta1).add_(grad, alpha=1 - beta1)\n","                exp_avg_sq.mul_(beta2).addcmul_(grad, grad, value=1 - beta2)\n","\n","                denom = exp_avg_sq.sqrt().add_(group['eps'])\n","\n","                correction1 = 1 - beta1**state['step']\n","                correction2 = 1 - beta2**state['step']\n","                step_size = group['lr'] * math.sqrt(correction2) / correction1\n","                # correction2 is a float thus math.sqrt is used\n","\n","                p.data.addcdiv_(exp_avg, denom, value=-step_size)\n","                \"\"\"\n","        return loss"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"7Ue0rgvkiAxz"},"source":["## Final project: add a schedular"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":16,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":6,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264367330,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"OENi5hp3iAxz"},"outputs":[],"source":["from torch.optim.lr_scheduler import ReduceLROnPlateau, _LRScheduler\n","\n","class MinimalScheduler(_LRScheduler):\n","    def __init__(self,\n","                 optimizer,\n","                 last_epoch=-1):\n","        \"\"\"\n","        Implements a minimal learning rate scheduler\n","        \"\"\"\n","        super().__init__(optimizer, last_epoch)\n","\n","    def get_lr(self):\n","        # Implement your logic here to return a list of learning rates for each param group\n","        # Example: return [group['lr'] * 0.9 for group in self.optimizer.param_groups]\n","        return [group['lr'] for group in self.optimizer.param_groups]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Uh7lY2VZiAxz"},"source":["# Training"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":17,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":12,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264367344,"user":{"displayName":"Roman Hunter","userId":"04599973894551074078"},"user_tz":360},"id":"LLkWiRLriAxz","outputId":"8d9bafd7-3670-4ab7-de4a-8eb5c4629121"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["cpu\n"]}],"source":["device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n","print(device) # should be cuda if GPU is enabled"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":86,"status":"ok","timestamp":1766264367431,"user":{"dis